stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> Open : create() — status defaults to "Open" (DB DEFAULT 'Open')

    Open --> Closed : close(closedBy) — sets closedBy / closedAt
    Open --> Cancelled : cancel()

    Closed --> Open : PUT /class-sessions/{id} with session_status=Open (update allows a direct status swap, bypassing open())
    Cancelled --> Open : PUT /class-sessions/{id} with session_status=Open

    note right of Open
        open() can never succeed: it rejects "already Open" and also
        rejects Closed/Cancelled, which are the only other allowed values.
        Reopening happens exclusively through PUT update.
    end note

    note right of Closed
        close() and cancel() guard against their own state and against
        each other, so Closed --> Cancelled and Cancelled --> Closed
        are rejected with 400. DELETE removes the row physically
        (no @SQLDelete soft delete despite deleted_at existing).
    end note

    Open --> [*] : DELETE (physical delete)
    Closed --> [*] : DELETE (physical delete)
    Cancelled --> [*] : DELETE (physical delete)
